NOTICE: attribution for the kafka-sre-fact-entries-v4 dataset

This dataset holds entries_index.jsonl (7,028 fact entries) and kb_entries.json (the record of that file).

THE ENTRIES ARE MODEL-WRITTEN. They were written from documentation chunks of the projects listed below by a locally
run language model (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, prompt kbe/5), and checked against the chunk by a second locally run language
model (GLM-5.3-Flash, prompt kbc/4). The title, the statement and the applies_when text of an entry are restatements
by the model, not text of the documentation. The quoted spans (at most 300 characters each) are verbatim from the chunk;
the heading trail, the lead-in line and the source path are taken from the chunk by code. Entries are not documentation,
may be partial, and are not a primary source. They are not endorsed by the Apache Software Foundation or the Strimzi
authors.

Audit result: an independent audit rated 200 accepted entries drawn from the 7,028: 178 ok (89.0 %, 90 % interval 84.7 %
to 92.4 %), 22 partial, 0 wrong. A second rater agreed on 50 of 50 re-rated entries. The bar fixed before the audit was
190 of 200 (95 %); it was not met. After the result the bar was changed to 80 % for this release only, and 178 of 200
passes that. The 22 partial entries drop a condition, a version or a scope, which can mislead a reader.

